  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Target gain scales from NIF's demonstrated ~4× to the ~45× total scientific gain (capsule gain ~375×) required at 10 MJ laser energy — unvalidated extrapolation from NIF Hybrid-E physics",
      "DPSSL laser driver achieves 10% wall-plug efficiency at 10 MJ / 10 Hz continuous operation, versus NIF's ~0.1% single-shot baseline",
      "Laser diode cost reduction from current ~$0.02/W floor to the ~$0.007/W TRUMPF/LLNL viability threshold — roughly 3× below current price floor",
      "Target factory mass-produces 864,000 cryogenic DT targets per day at <$1/target (marginally above the $0.75 Goodin economic limit at 450 MJ/shot)",
      "Final optics survive commercial repetition rates and 14 MeV neutron fluence — no validated solution exists beyond NIF's $40M/yr single-shot refurbishment baseline",
      "Liquid lithium first-wall pipes provide TBR > 1 and withstand 3–5 year chamber replacement intervals with no published nuclear analysis or engineering study",
      "Plant availability reaches 75% placeholder despite 3–5 year chamber replacement outages, versus OSIRIS/SOMBRERO 1992 historical anchor of ~68–69%"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No superconducting magnet system — DPSSL laser driver replaces REBCO/HTS magnets as dominant capital item, eliminating cryoplant and large-scale cryogenics",
      "No plasma-facing components requiring remote handling for routine steady-state maintenance (pulsed operation shifts the maintenance model)",
      "Lower regulatory burden than fission — 2023 NRC decision to regulate fusion under 10 CFR Part 30 avoids the 2.2× fission-style building cost markup",
      "Liquid lithium blanket is inexpensive vs. FLiBe alternatives — CAS27 special materials only $8M given abundant Li supply chain (vs. Xcimer's 940 t FLiBe inventory with beryllium/Li-6 constraints)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Laser driver capital ($3,000M central at $300/J × 10 MJ, range $1,400M–$8,500M) — no analogue in the rest of the fusion landscape and the dominant CAS22 line item",
      "Target factory producing 864,000 cryogenic DT targets/day with tritium handling and cryogenic layering at throughput (NOAK ~$97M baseline; FOAK premium 3–10× unquantified)",
      "Final optics refurbishment/replacement at commercial fluence — NIF baseline $40M/yr; no validated commercial-rep-rate solution exists",
      "Chamber replacement capex every 3–5 years driven by pulsed neutron damage and ablation — implies extended planned outages absent in steady-state plants",
      "Ash clearing and target injection synchronization at 10 Hz — no published engineering study or cost model for Inertia's liquid-Li-adjacent architecture"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Capsule gain G > 50–100 required for viability has not been experimentally demonstrated; NIF peak is 4.13 and Xcimer's G=65/200 projections are simulation-only",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Plant availability is the single largest LCOE driver (elasticity −0.97); 75% placeholder is unvalidated and historical IFE anchors (OSIRIS/SOMBRERO) sit at ~68–69%, while Inertia's 3–5 yr chamber replacement implies ~55–60%",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Laser driver cost is dominant and poorly bounded — true elasticity ~+0.4 via LASER_COST_PER_J override (not the +0.045 shown in the sensitivity table); scenario sweep produces LCOE range $79.7–$160.5",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Final optics survivability at commercial repetition rates is TRL ~2 with no validated >10⁷-shot solution for any IFE concept",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Laser diode price must fall from ~$0.02/W to ~$0.007/W for economic viability; at 10 MJ / 10% WPE / 10 Hz the diode bill alone is ~$2B at current floor",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Inertia has no published plant-level capital cost breakdown, no TBR analysis for the liquid Li blanket, and no ash-clearing strategy — multiple blocking proprietary gaps",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Target cost goal of <$1/target is marginally over the $0.75 Goodin economic limit at 450 MJ/shot and 13.6 ¢/kWh; neither company has published a manufacturing process at 864,000 targets/day throughput",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Driver lifetime/reliability (Hawker Pearson −0.134) dominates over unit cost (+0.075); 30M-shot commercial threshold = only ~35 days at 10 Hz continuous operation",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium supply chain: global inventory ~25–30 kg from declining CANDU fleet constrains fleet-scale D-T deployment even if startup tritium is available from U.S. stockpiles",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Thermal cycle ambiguity — Inertia cites steam (Rankine ~35%) while Xcimer's IFE Workshop 2022 materials cite helium Brayton 45%; website/paper conflict unresolved",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Xcimer Vulcan (12 MJ KrF) is the key technical validation milestone and not targeted until 2030 — amplifiers would be 'the largest laser amplifiers ever built'",
        "severity": "medium"
      }
    ]
  },
